Figure 6 demonstrates how Nano-11 improves antigen targeting to immunopotentiating cells in the draining lymph node and enhances antigen retention at the injection site. Panel A shows that OVA-containing migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) exhibit the highest expression of the costimulatory molecule CD86. Panel B characterizes OVA-positive MigDCs, indicating a significant presence of OVA within CD11b+ DC subsets. Panel C, utilizing in vivo imaging, illustrates that Alexa Fluor 647-labeled OVA formulated with Nano-11 or aluminum hydroxide is retained at the injection site for a prolonged period, whereas soluble OVA clears rapidly by day 2, highlighting Nano-11's role in extending antigen availability.